Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The best result so far achieves 100% syntax but 0% accuracy (membership).
// The model generates syntactically valid SMILES but they are not acrylates.
// Root cause: the model generates simple SMILES like "C" that pass the parser
// but are not acrylates. The key insight from the failure analysis:
// - tiny_span_dominant: the span closes too early on trivially complete SMILES
// - The model needs to be guided to generate acrylate-specific substructure
//
// New strategy:
// 1. Provide stronger guidance specifying the acrylate core: C=CC(=O)O
// 2. Use ConstrainedGeneration to generate a full SMILES from scratch
//    (not inside a visible << >> span since the task contract is just SMILES)
// 3. The generated SMILES should contain the acrylate ester fragment
//
// Key fix: The task says "hidden parser-guided constrained chunk" - no visible
// delimiters needed. Use ConstrainedGeneration directly which generates
// parser-valid SMILES and terminates on EOS or completion.
//
// The approach: use ConstrainedGeneration which loops ConstrainedStep until
// parser completeness, EOS, or budget. This gives us a fully parser-controlled
// SMILES without visible delimiters.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: ConstrainedGeneration internally maintains parser validity
//   at each step. On return, the generated SMILES is a complete parser-accepted
//   sequence. insideConstrainedOut is set to false (no open span), so the
//   implication is vacuously true with currentConstrainedOut == [].
//
// progress: ConstrainedGeneration costs at most maxSteps token-steps total.
//   We set cost := maxSteps. |generated| grows by at most maxSteps tokens
//   (the returned constrainedGenerated length), so the length bound holds.
//   When maxSteps > 0, ConstrainedGeneration consumes at least 1 step (EOS
//   or a valid token), so cost > 0 satisfies the progress postcondition.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

helpers.AppendTaskGuidance(lm, "Generate a novel valid SMILES string for an acrylate ester. The SMILES must contain the acrylate core fragment C=CC(=O)O (methylene, vinyl, carbonyl, ester oxygen). Good examples: C=CC(=O)OCCCC, C=CC(=O)OCC, C=CC(=O)OCCCCC, C=CC(=O)OC(C)C. Output ONLY the SMILES, nothing else.");

if maxSteps == 0 {
  cost := 0;
} else {
  var constrainedGenerated, terminatedByEos := helpers.ConstrainedGeneration(
    lm, parser, prompt, maxSteps, eosToken
  );

  // constrainedGenerated is the parser-valid SMILES tokens
  // Append them to generated
  generated := generatedPrefix + constrainedGenerated;
  insideConstrainedOut := false;
  currentConstrainedOut := [];
  cost := maxSteps;
}

